window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Thirty-six-year-old Daphne Silver thought she finally had it all; she was married to the love of her life, had an amazing job, and was the mother to three beautiful children. From leading The Hot Moms Book Club to running to after-school practices, nothing could stop her from living the perfectly normal life she had dreamed of, not even her ADHD.</p> <p>That is, until the accident.</p> <p>Now, she’s left with only two of those.</p> <p>Trying desperately to cling to the life she built, she signs up for a technology-free retreat.</p> <p>But it seems the stars have other plans for her. Instead of leaving for her trip, she is pulled into a world full of fae, dragons, and magic. After a handsome stranger, Silas, rescues her from imminent danger, he agrees to help her get home. They embark on a journey navigating Daphne’s newfound magic, a budding romance that could never work, and the vague predictions of oracles.</p> <p>With no one looking for her, Daphne has two weeks to find a way back to her world—she can’t allow her family to suffer two tragedies in less than a year.</p> <p>But in a world full of magic and mystery, will she be able to make it back?</p>"; 
